codeSplitters agents: Stop a running agent, and pass a note into its next run
Follow-up to the claims PR. There's no way to stop a run: agent-routes.ts has only GET/POST. Add a Stop button on the run card (needs an abort endpoint: kill the local process / cancel the hosted container run, release its claim, mark it stopped). Add a "tell it" note: a running CLI can't take messages, so the note goes into its next re-run's prompt, the same way taskPrompt already passes conflicts. With 1000 runs on a file, the Agents panel also needs bulk actions (stop all on these lines / of this harness).
