codeSplitter merge: settle an edit to a line the other side joined or wrapped
Found by the merge replay of 14 hand-fixed "merge main" commits (`apps/codesplitter/docs/merge-solutions.md` §10). Two cards a rule would settle exactly like the person did.

**What happens.** One side joins two lines into one, or wraps one line onto two. The other side edits the same statement. The ids no longer line up one to one, so it's a card, though the word-level edits don't touch.

**#1214 `d7ffea8`, `apps/git-recon/src/ui/main.ts` L707 (a join)**

```ts
// base
net.mirror.frame(dt, input);
net.battle.input(input, now);
// main: an argument added
net.battle.input(input, now, net.mirror.acked);
// branch: the two lines joined
net.battle.input(net.mirror.frame(dt, input), now);
// the fix
net.battle.input(net.mirror.frame(dt, input), now, net.mirror.acked);
```

**#1191 `0ebf5e2`, `apps/codesplitter/src/openapi.ts` L317 (a wrap)**

Both sides added a last field to one `ok: obj({ … })` literal: main `regenerated: arr(…)` on the line, the branch `took: arr(…)` on a new continuation line. The fix is main's line, then the branch's continuation line.

